# Li wall of LTX-beta as in the S3X-EIRENE run. EIRENE semantics for the
# recycling coefficient R = 0.5 (S3X eirene_coupling.txt): prompt TRIM
# reflection with the unscaled R_N(E,theta) of EIRENE's H_on_Li_1.00 table
# (processes.h5 /surface/reflection/h_on_li), then a fraction 1-R retained,
# and the remainder R - R_N returned thermally at the wall temperature, 95 %
# as H2. The lottery of surf_react surface/pwi uses absolute cumulative
# probabilities, so the order T, R, A gives a total return of max(R_N, R),
# atoms R_N and molecules R - R_N. The S3X balance confirms it: of the 0.5 x
# 6.34e20 /s returned, 45 % come back as fast atoms (R_N ~ 0.22 at ~100 eV).
# Li sputtering by the H atoms that hit the wall is additive (S channel).

# H+ from the plasma (handed over by fix surface/emit/recycle ... pwi)
H+ --> H
T h_on_li

H+ --> NULL
R 0.5

H+ --> H2 + H
A 1.0 0.95

# H atoms: same pipeline, plus physical sputtering of the Li wall
H --> H
T h_on_li

H --> NULL
R 0.5

H --> H2
A 1.0 0.95

H --> Li
S H_on_Li

# H2: no molecular reflection table, half retained, half returned as H2
H2 --> NULL
R 0.5

H2 --> H2
A 1.0

# H2+ test ions neutralise as thermal H2
H2+ --> H2
A 1.0

# Li atoms that come back to the wall stick
Li --> Li
A 0.0
